  "name": "TeamRetro: Post an AI standup digest to Slack and escalate stale blockers",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "tr1600-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -400,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 720,
        "height": 700,
        "content": "## TeamRetro: Post an AI standup digest to Slack and escalate stale blockers\n\nFor team leads who want the standup in Slack without a wall of text. When a TeamRetro standup closes, OpenAI writes a short headline with highlights, the blockers are listed underneath, and everyone's full updates go into a thread. A blocker carried over for several standups is raised separately with the team lead.\n\n### How it works\n\n1. The TeamRetro Trigger fires on **Standup Completed** with every update in the payload, so no API key is needed. A delivery TeamRetro retries is skipped, so nothing happens twice.\n2. A Code node turns the updates into Slack formatting and counts how many standups each blocker has been open.\n3. OpenAI writes the headline, highlights and watch-outs from only what the team wrote.\n4. Slack posts the digest, then the per-person detail as a thread reply.\n5. Blockers open `staleAfter` standups go to the lead channel, then again every `staleAfter` more.\n\n### Setup\n\n- [ ] Copy the Production URL from \"When Standup Closes\" into TeamRetro under Settings \u2192 Integrations \u2192 Webhooks, tick **Standup Completed**, and paste the signing secret back into the trigger\n- [ ] Set `teamChannel`, `leadChannel` and `staleAfter` in \"Settings\"\n- [ ] Add your OpenAI and Slack credentials. Sample data is pinned, so Execute workflow runs end to end\n\nRunning the pinned sample a second time stops at \"Skip Repeat Deliveries\": that is the duplicate guard.\n\n### Customization\n\nMatch `blockerTopic` to your blocker question; the default catches any question containing \"block\". Edit the system message to change the digest's tone."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "tr1600-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
